  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (sentiment ≤ 0.00) to counteract overestimation bias.",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1-2 days if recent price spikes are followed by strong sentiment reversal.",
    "Apply mean reversion correction: if forecast is > 10% above recent 7-day average, reduce by 5-10%.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if sentiment history shows sustained negative sentiment (e.g., 3+ consecutive negative entries).",
    "Avoid over-optimistic forecasts after sharp price spikes; cap forecast at 10% below peak observed in last 10 days.",
    "If sentiment is positive (≥ 0.25), allow slight upward bias but cap at 5% above recent 30-day average to prevent overshoot."
  ]
}
